course: dictionary
lesson: 15828
title: Underestimate: guessing too low
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To underestimate something is to guess it is smaller than it really is. The prefix under means too little, so an underestimate is a guess that is too low. «I underestimated how long the walk would take.» The walk took longer than the guess, so the guess was too low.
explain: You can also underestimate a person. It means you think they are less clever, strong or able than they really are. «The little team underestimated the big team, and they lost the match.» The little team thought the big team was weaker than it was, and that was their mistake.
explain: Underestimate can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, it is an action: you underestimate. As a noun, it is the guess itself: «My guess of ten sweets was an underestimate, because there were twenty.» Look at the words around it to see which one it is.
fact: Underestimate means to guess that something is smaller than it really is.
fact: «Underestimate» can also mean to think someone is less able than they really are.
fact: The prefix «under» means too little, so an underestimate is a guess that is too low.
fact: In maths, rounding down can give an underestimate, because the answer you get is lower than the true answer.
fact: «Never underestimate» is a common phrase, as in «Never underestimate your opponent.»

exercise: «I underestimated how long the walk would take.» What does underestimated mean here? | *Guessed it would be shorter than it really was | Measured it exactly | Forgot to start the walk | Guessed it would be longer than it really was
exercise: «The little team underestimated the big team.» What did the little team think? | They wanted to join the big team | *They thought the big team was weaker than it really was | They thought the big team was stronger than it really was | They cheered for the big team
exercise: «My guess of ten sweets was an underestimate.» What was wrong with the guess? | *It was too low | It was exactly right | It was too high | It was not a number

test: Ali guesses there are 30 cakes, but there are 45. What is Ali's guess? | A word for a shape | Exactly right | *An underestimate | An overestimate
test: Which phrase warns you not to think someone is weaker than they are? | *Never underestimate someone | Always overestimate someone | Ignore someone | Forget someone's name

exam: Which is an underestimate? | Timing the walk with a clock | Guessing 20 minutes for a walk that took 5 minutes | Guessing 20 minutes for a walk that took 20 minutes | *Guessing 5 minutes for a walk that took 20 minutes
